🚀 Day 02: PowerShell Objects, Pipelines & Filtering

Today, I continued my 10-day PowerShell learning challenge, focusing on PowerShell objects, pipelines, filtering, and sorting in Windows Server 2022.

 📌 Key Learning Areas

- Understanding PowerShell Objects.
- Exploring object properties and methods using `Get-Member`.
- Using the Pipeline (`|`) to connect commands.
- Selecting specific properties with `Select-Object`.
- Filtering data with `Where-Object`.
- Sorting data using `Sort-Object`.

 💻 Hands-on Practical Labs

 Lab 1: PowerShell Objects

```powershell
Get-Service | Get-Member
```

Explored PowerShell object properties and methods.

 Lab 2: PowerShell Pipeline

```powershell
Get-Service | Select-Object Name, Status, StartType
```

Practiced passing service objects through the pipeline and selecting specific properties.

 Lab 3: Filtering & Sorting

```powershell
Get-Service | Where-Object {$_.Status -eq 'Running'}

Get-Service | Where-Object {$_.Status -eq 'Stopped'}

Get-Service | Sort-Object Name
```

Practiced filtering Windows services by status and sorting them alphabetically.

